  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.distinction":
    "Unlike source-merge, premises remain separate and readable as reasons rather than moving as data into a destination. The deck and relationship text distinguish logical support from transport or aggregation.",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.domains.0": "Argument structure",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.goodFor.0":
    "Explain why a recommendation follows from stated reasons",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.goodFor.1":
    "Connect evidence to a qualified conclusion",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.goodFor.2":
    "Summarize an argument before the next chapter",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.intent":
    "Show which stated reasons support an authored conclusion.",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.motionBeats.0":
    "Establish the authored starting arrangement.",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.motionBeats.1":
    "Two or three premise strips arrive separately along the lower third. Their ends extend and join into a single bridge deck, with a central connector label appearing only once the premises are readable. The conclusion rises onto that deck and holds above all visible premises. Nothing is transported through the bridge; it is an explicit visual model of an argument's support.",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.motionBeats.2":
    "Hold the resolved authored relationships before the shared exit.",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.name": "From reasons to conclusion",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.notFor.0":
    "The renderer does not prove validity, establish causality, or derive a conclusion.",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.notFor.1":
    "At most three concise reasons fit the six-second argument.",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.notFor.2":
    "Support geometry is rhetorical and carries no confidence score or evidence weight.",
  "motionAtlas.argument-bridge.prompt":
    'Use Motion Atlas "From reasons to conclusion" (argument-bridge) as a conceptual graphic. Show which stated reasons support an authored conclusion. Replace fictional sample content with approved authored content before making product claims.',
