  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.description":
    "A compact table reveals explicit capability states one line at a time, then holds an authored row or column focus. Supported, unavailable, conditional, and unknown states remain visually distinct.",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.distinction":
    "The grid carries a two-dimensional comparison contract and four explicit cell meanings. It is neither a cohort dot-matrix nor source-to-destination schema-mapping, and its choreography compares each line item across all alternatives.",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.domains.0": "Comparative reasoning",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.goodFor.0":
    "Compare feature support across a small set of alternatives",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.goodFor.1": "Explain what each plan includes",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.goodFor.2":
    "Separate conditional support from unknown information",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.goodFor.3":
    "Compare task needs with an explicitly supplied capability set",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.goodFor.4":
    "Explain fit across affordability, usability, and lifecycle coverage",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.goodFor.5":
    "Show whether affordability and defined quality requirements are both met in an authored example",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.goodFor.6":
    "Compare local and network-dependent operations",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.goodFor.7":
    "Show unknown or planned capability support honestly",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.intent":
    "Compare alternatives using the same explicit list of capabilities.",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.motionBeats.0":
    "The labeled setup establishes the authored comparison.",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.motionBeats.1":
    "A table skeleton and option headings settle first. A narrow horizontal rule advances through the capability rows, resolving all cells in each row together so the audience compares like with like. The final focus opens a bracket around one selected column or row while every other cell remains legible, followed by the common opaque exit.",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.motionBeats.2":
    "Both sides remain readable in the resolved hold.",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.name": "Capability by capability",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.notFor.0":
    "Cells are categorical statements, not performance scores or quantities.",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.notFor.1":
    "Unknown must never be rendered as absent, and conditional cells require meaningful source qualifications.",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.notFor.2":
    "At most three options and five rows fit the intended six-second overview.",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.notFor.3":
    "A capability state is a supplied statement about a specific context and version. Do not infer market-wide absence, universal superiority, or current competitor support from a strategic comparison.",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.notFor.4":
    "Qualitative affordability requires a stated audience and context; included features are not proof that a plan is affordable to every team.",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.notFor.5":
    "A quality row needs an explicit criterion and source. Included affordability and quality cells do not prove that every organization can afford the tool or that it is safe.",
  "motionAtlas.capability-matrix.notFor.6":
    "Unavailable, conditional and unknown must stay distinct. Planned capability is not currently supported.",
