    "Demo clinic A",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.default.reference.sourceLabel":
    "Fictional rate sheet A",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.description":
    "A fictional invoice line is laid over a separate price reference. Only matching procedure, provider, payer, period, and quantity windows permit the amounts to align on one scale; an unmatched context leaves the comparison unresolved.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.distinction":
    "Unlike benefit-shortfall-correction, no payment is corrected and no unpaid amount is treated as an entitlement. Unlike paired-contrast, exact context keys govern whether a numeric comparison is allowed. Unlike keyed-row-zipper, the records remain separate and open an amount ruler rather than becoming a joined dataset.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.domains.0":
    "Reference reconciliation",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.goodFor.0":
    "Explain why published prices need the same billing context",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.goodFor.1":
    "Support a fictional price-transparency investigation",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.goodFor.2":
    "Show a discrepancy for review without implying a refund or legal entitlement",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.intent":
    "Make the context required for a monetary comparison explicit before showing a difference.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.motionBeats.0":
    "Reveal separate billed and reference lines.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.motionBeats.1":
    "Register context windows with visible mismatch notches.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.motionBeats.2":
    "Matching contexts open common-scale rulers and optional difference.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.motionBeats.3":
    "Hold sources and unresolved or matched context.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.motionBeats.4": "Shared opaque exit.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.name":
    "Match the reference before comparing a charge",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.notFor.0":
    "This is a fictional one-line comparison. It is not a medical billing interpretation, legal determination, price guarantee, negotiation result, or refund claim.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.notFor.1":
    "Totals use exact integer arithmetic in the shared smallest unit. The signed difference may be negative, positive, or zero; no automatic favorable result is implied.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.notFor.2":
    "A mismatch in any context key or quantity leaves the comparison unresolved. Similar text is not treated as a match, and no real CPT or payer taxonomy is inferred.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.notFor.3":
    "The ruler uses a common zero and a domain derived from the larger supplied total. For two zero totals use a one-minor-unit display domain without changing either value.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.notFor.4":
    "Currency, quantities, source label, period, and fictional status stay visible at the resolved hold. Published reference prices can have qualifications outside this bounded example.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.notFor.5":
    "Supplied prose meaning, fictional status and agreement with structured choices are authoring responsibilities. Runtime validation enforces structure, numeric bounds, identities and references.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.notFor.literal-whitespace":
    "Exact context values render whitespace as distinct amber underlined marks. Input values, accessible labels and equality remain unchanged.",
  "motionAtlas.charge-reference-alignment.prompt":
    'Use Motion Atlas "Match the reference before comparing a charge" (charge-reference-alignment) as a conceptual graphic. Make the context required for a monetary comparison explicit before showing a difference. Replace fictional examples with approved authored content before making product claims.',
