  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.creativeDirection":
    "Within six seconds, reveal two or three modest service entrances and a participant considering their labels. The participant points to the configured choice. At that entrance, either unfold a ramp over the step or roll a physical obstruction clear, according to the supplied access change; the staff member holds the door while the participant moves under their own power through it. Keep the other service options visible, hold the selected doorway and cleared path, then apply the shared opaque exit fade.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.default.labels.choice": "Chosen service",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.default.labels.participant":
    "Example participant",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.default.labels.staff": "Service team",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.default.scenarioCaption":
    "Fictional access example",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.default.services.0.label":
    "Example shelter desk",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.default.services.1.label":
    "Example information",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.description":
    "A participant chooses a named community service and an access barrier is visibly addressed at its entrance. The person then approaches and enters by the accessible path shown in the example.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.distinction":
    "The central transformation changes physical access to a doorway, followed by participant-directed entry. It is not node-traversal, a generic status transition, or merely labels arriving on cards.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.domains.0": "Access and participation",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.goodFor.0":
    "Explain a fictional barrier to accessing shelter or community support",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.goodFor.1":
    "Show the combination of service choice and a usable entrance",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.goodFor.2":
    "Introduce an accessibility improvement through a physical action",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.intent":
    "Show that a service becomes usable when a person can choose it and physically reach its entrance.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.motionBeats.0":
    "Reveal options. Participant points toward the authored choice.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.motionBeats.1":
    "Staff unfolds the selected ramp or clears its obstruction and holds the door.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.motionBeats.2":
    "Participant walks or self-propels through the selected entrance.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.motionBeats.3":
    "Hold the usable chosen path with all other options visible.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.motionBeats.4":
    "Return to the opaque ground through the shared envelope.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.name": "Open the service someone chooses",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.notFor.0":
    "The ramp and entrance are conceptual silhouettes, not dimensional design guidance or a certification of accessibility.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.notFor.1":
    "Removing one depicted physical barrier does not imply that language, eligibility, safety, affordability, or other barriers have been resolved.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.notFor.2":
    "Entry into a shelter desk does not imply a shelter placement, admission entitlement, or guaranteed housing.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.notFor.3":
    "The scene shows one fictional participant; it makes no population-level access or impact claim.",
  "motionAtlas.chosen-service-access.prompt":
    "Open the service someone chooses. Show that a service becomes usable when a person can choose it and physically reach its entrance.",
