  "motionAtlas.component-material-return.motionBeats.1":
    "Reveal the returned assembly within its stated material boundary. An operator separates its labeled parts into their supplied reuse, repair, recycling and residue destinations. Separately labeled replacement inputs join the recovered parts in the new assembly. Hold the new assembly, recycling and residue with an input-output mass equation, then fade.",
  "motionAtlas.component-material-return.motionBeats.2":
    "Hold conserved quantities and visible destinations. The outer envelope returns to ground.",
  "motionAtlas.component-material-return.name":
    "Recover parts, account for residue",
  "motionAtlas.component-material-return.notFor.0":
    "Returned mass + replacement input = reassembled mass + recycling-stream mass + residue. Reassembled mass includes reuse and repair routes without assuming mass loss.",
  "motionAtlas.component-material-return.notFor.1":
    "Sent to recycling is not the same as recovered secondary material. No recovery yield, virgin-material displacement, embodied-carbon saving or infinite recyclability is claimed.",
  "motionAtlas.component-material-return.notFor.2":
    "Repair success and component compatibility are authored assumptions in this fictional example. Additional process inputs or losses require extending the supplied boundary, not silently discarding mass.",
