  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.description":
    "Place-time strips reveal which recorded visits overlap a supplied investigation window. Unknown times remain unresolved, and overlap never becomes an inferred transmission link.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.distinction":
    "Unlike network-graph, node-traversal, or line-trace, the hero action is a window stencil intersecting interval lengths attached to people and a physical venue. No traveling signal implies transmission.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.domains.0": "Time and place intersection",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.goodFor.0":
    "Explain how an investigation filters recorded presence by time and place.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.goodFor.1":
    "Distinguish temporal overlap from proof of exposure or transmission.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.goodFor.2":
    "Show why missing visit times remain unresolved.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.intent":
    "Explain the difference between sharing a place and being recorded there during the same defined window.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.motionBeats.0":
    "Establish the supplied identities and setting.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.motionBeats.1":
    "Reveal the shared place above the supplied person-specific time ribbons. Position the authored intervals on one axis and lower the investigation-window stencil over them; outline only actual interval intersections. Hold overlapping, nonoverlapping and unknown records alongside the same people, then fade. The intersection represents a review candidate, not a confirmed transmission.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.motionBeats.2":
    "Hold the authored final records and derived quantities.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.motionBeats.3":
    "Return to the opaque ground through the shared envelope.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.name": "Shared place, overlapping time",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.notFor.0":
    "The denominator is records.length, one record per distinct person in this bounded example. Overlap + no overlap + unknown equals that denominator; counts are derived from interval intersection.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.notFor.1":
    "Intervals and the supplied investigation window use half-open bounds [start,end), so touching endpoints alone do not count as overlap. Unknown means both bounds are null.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.notFor.2":
    "Any overlap is only recorded co-presence under the supplied window. It is not a case definition, exposure determination, disease-specific contact rule, causal link, or medical recommendation.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.notFor.3":
    "The time axis is a fictional relative scale, not an epidemiological duration. No transmission arrows or infection probabilities may be added.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.prompt":
    "Use Shared place, overlapping time (contact-window-overlap) for a fictional or approved authored example. Explain the difference between sharing a place and being recorded there during the same defined window.",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.tags.0": "outbreak investigation",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.tags.1": "contact window",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.tags.2": "temporal overlap",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.tags.3": "shared location",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.tags.4": "presence interval",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.tags.5": "timeline intersection",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.tags.6": "uncertain records",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.tags.7": "contact tracing",
  "motionAtlas.contact-window-overlap.useWhen":
    "Explain the difference between sharing a place and being recorded there during the same defined window.",
