  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.controls.weaveStart": "weaveStart",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.controls.weaveStart.help":
    "Choose the first crossing pattern; subsequent crossings alternate consistently without changing contributor roles.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.controls.weaveStart.over-first": "over-first",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.controls.weaveStart.under-first":
    "under-first",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.controls.weft": "weft",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.controls.weft.help":
    "Horizontal contributions woven in array order. Each item owns one shuttle pass and one final band.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.creativeDirection":
    "Reveal a small loom frame with two or three vertical bands and the same bounded set of horizontal shuttles. Tension the vertical contributions first; sweep each horizontal shuttle once through an alternating over-under mask so the crossing pattern visibly locks together. Keep a short labeled end of every contributor's band outside the frame. Hold the finished fabric with all identities still traceable, then fade the complete textile within the six-second envelope.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.default.copy.example":
    "Fictional collaboration",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.default.copy.result":
    "Example shared field guide",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.default.warp.0.label": "Example structure",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.default.warp.1.label": "Example facts",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.default.weft.0.label": "Example wording",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.default.weft.1.label": "Example layout",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.description":
    "Named contributions become a woven surface while keeping their own visible thread patterns. Their interdependence is shown by alternating over-and-under crossings rather than convergence into a hub.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.distinction":
    "Source-merge collapses inputs toward a destination. This creates alternating physical interlocks, preserves every contribution through the finished structure, and uses neither nodes nor connecting paths.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.domains.0": "Editorial explanation",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.goodFor.0":
    "Explain complementary work becoming one shared deliverable",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.goodFor.1":
    "Illustrate an editorial, design, or workshop collaboration",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.goodFor.2":
    "Show contributions staying attributable inside a collective result",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.goodFor.3":
    "Explain sector-wide co-creation without erasing contributor identity",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.goodFor.4":
    "Show partnership without a central savior",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.intent":
    "Show that a shared result depends on distinct contributions that remain identifiable.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.motionBeats.0":
    "Reveal the loom and tension vertical bands.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.motionBeats.1":
    "Each horizontal shuttle crosses once in array order.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.motionBeats.2":
    "Hold alternating crossings with traceable contributor ends.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.name": "Distinct Work, Shared Fabric",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.notFor.0":
    "Band count is the exact number of supplied contributions. Equal band width is decorative and does not represent equal effort, value, ownership, or impact.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.notFor.1":
    "Over-under order is a weave construction, not a ranking of contributors or a chronology of all real work.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.notFor.2":
    "The scene is not a dependency graph or proof of conflict-free collaborative editing. Suppressing contributor ends reduces attribution clarity.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.notFor.3":
    "The weave is a relationship metaphor. Thread widths and crossings do not quantify labor, ownership, compensation or social impact.",
  "motionAtlas.contribution-weave.prompt":
    "Show that a shared result depends on distinct contributions that remain identifiable.",
