  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.default.labels.nonNumeric":
    "Not numeric",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.default.labels.plotted": "Plotted",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.default.labels.range": "Out of range",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.default.labels.total":
    "All supplied rows",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.description":
    "Coordinate rows pass explicit numeric and range checks before they become points. Invalid or missing coordinates remain in visible reason trays instead of disappearing from the denominator.",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.distinction":
    "Unlike cell-normalization, rejected values are not automatically repaired. This is a coordinate-specific validation with complete dropped-row accounting and no silent removal.",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.domains.0":
    "Geospatial data validation",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.goodFor.0":
    "Explain coordinate row-loss diagnostics",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.goodFor.1":
    "Show rejected mapping rows without losing the denominator",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.intent":
    "Account for every input row before plotting coordinates.",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.name":
    "Account for the rows that cannot be mapped",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.notFor.0":
    "Latitude must be numeric within [-90,90] and longitude within [-180,180], endpoints inclusive. Check missing first, then numeric type, then range. These global coordinate-validity bounds are fixed invariants, not editable options.",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.notFor.1":
    "Passing numeric/range checks does not establish that a location is correct.",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.notFor.2":
    "Possible latitude/longitude swaps, null-island and DMS parsing require separate qualified checks and are not silently corrected here.",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.notFor.3":
    "Graticule is a schematic coordinate plane, not a map of real places.",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.notFor.4":
    "No live geography, online routing, JSX, functions, URLs, private records or external requests. Maps are schematic local plans; no real-world inference follows.",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.notFor.5":
    "Authored prose must identify schematic geography and accurately describe the selected example. Runtime validation preserves supplied prose and checks explicit structural and numeric rules without natural-language classification.",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.prompt":
    "React/SVG 960x600 canvas, shared palette, deterministic 180 frames at 30fps. This is schematic local geography with no real basemap. Frames 0-12 reveal. Frames 13-50 line up coordinate rows beside latitude and longitude rulers. Frames 51-105 evaluate each row; valid pairs plot on a schematic graticule while failed rows move into labeled missing/type/range trays. Frames 106-139 hold plotted and rejected counts that reconcile to input. Hold at frames 140-165; fade to the same opaque ground at frames 166-179 for an editorial loop.",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.tags.0": "coordinate validation",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.tags.1": "row loss",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.tags.2": "missing coordinates",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.tags.3": "range checks",
  "motionAtlas.coordinate-quality-triage.useWhen":
    "Account for every input row before plotting coordinates.",
