    "The authored setup is established.",
  "motionAtlas.disclosure-aperture.motionBeats.1":
    "Reveal one local document behind a tall boundary panel and an empty disclosure envelope outside it. Each authored share field briefly lifts as a duplicate while the original stays printed; a precisely sized aperture opens only opposite that field and lets its duplicate pass into the envelope. Retained fields never lift or leave. Close the aperture and hold the complete original beside the selected disclosure contents, then return to the opaque loop ground.",
  "motionAtlas.disclosure-aperture.motionBeats.2":
    "The completed authored state remains held.",
  "motionAtlas.disclosure-aperture.name": "Only the Chosen Fields Leave",
  "motionAtlas.disclosure-aperture.notFor.0":
    "Shared quantity is the number of fields marked share. Retained quantity is the number marked retain. Neither is a percentage of an unshown larger dataset.",
  "motionAtlas.disclosure-aperture.notFor.1":
    "All-retain and all-share inputs are valid but communicate no disclosure and complete disclosure respectively.",
  "motionAtlas.disclosure-aperture.notFor.2":
    "The animation does not perform redaction, access control, privacy review, or secure transport. It shows only an authored policy for the depicted fields.",
  "motionAtlas.disclosure-aperture.notFor.3":
    "A published summary field must already be approved and supplied. This preset neither computes safe aggregation nor proves anonymity, privacy, consent, or correct access control.",
  "motionAtlas.disclosure-aperture.notFor.4":
    "Public visibility of selected fields does not grant access to the underlying records or establish a customer-acquisition result.",
  "motionAtlas.disclosure-aperture.notFor.5":
    "Do not claim that clean detector output means the content is safe or anonymous.",
  "motionAtlas.disclosure-aperture.notFor.6":
    "All-retain represents declining the transfer; selected fields may include sensitive values.",
  "motionAtlas.disclosure-aperture.notFor.7":
    "Keeping file bytes local does not mean the remote system knows nothing about the dataset.",
