  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.description":
    "Keep the same people visible as a fictional multi-dose cohort returns for successive recorded visits. Missed and unobserved visits leave visible gaps instead of removing people from the denominator.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.distinction":
    "Unlike dot-matrix or status-cycle, each person retains identity across multiple visit gates, and missing observations stay spatially visible. Unlike missed-visit-reconnect, this compares the entire baseline cohort rather than the work of following up an already missed group.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.domains.0":
    "People over repeated visits",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.goodFor.0":
    "Explain retention across a fictional multi-dose programme.",
