    "Show how a missed visit differs from an unknown record or a visit not yet due.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.goodFor.2":
    "Keep the baseline cohort visible while comparing later attendance.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.intent":
    "Show who returned across visits without silently changing the population being compared.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.motionBeats.0":
    "Establish the supplied identities and setting.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.motionBeats.1":
    "Introduce the supplied cohort at the first visit arch. Slide later visit arches across the same identity lanes: a person enters an arch only when that visit is recorded, while missed, not-yet-due and unknown marks remain distinct. Hold the attendance fabric with separate visit numerators over one fixed cohort denominator before the opaque exit.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.motionBeats.2":
    "Hold the authored final records and derived quantities.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.motionBeats.3":
    "Return to the opaque ground through the shared envelope.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.name": "The same cohort returns",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.notFor.0":
    "The fixed baseline denominator is participants.length. Each per-visit recorded numerator counts participant records with that visit marked recorded; no population coverage or protection percentage is inferred.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.notFor.1":
    "Missing, missed, and not-yet-due are different supplied states. They are never auto-converted into clinical noncompliance or a recommendation.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.notFor.2":
    "Visit order is ordinal only. No elapsed time, vaccine name, interval, dose schedule, eligibility, or catch-up dosing advice is supplied.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.notFor.3":
    "Each participant occupies one lane throughout; a returning participant is not a newly added person. Arrays, not independent totals, own all counts.",
  "motionAtlas.dose-cohort-return-paths.prompt":
    "Use The same cohort returns (dose-cohort-return-paths) for a fictional or approved authored example. Show who returned across visits without silently changing the population being compared.",
