    "Item B3",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.default.groups.1.label":
    "Demo collection B",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.default.measure.basisLabel":
    "Illustrative stored bytes",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.description":
    "Two equal-count collections begin with matching item marks. Each item unfolds into a strip proportional to its supplied byte size, revealing different total data volumes on one common ruler without changing the item count.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.distinction":
    "Unlike capability-matrix, this changes the represented measure from a discrete count to item-weighted size. Unlike bar-race, no rank changes over time and no data values evolve. Unlike population-normalized-map, no denominator division or geographic fill is used; the animation opens each counted object to expose its unequal weight.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.domains.0": "Measurement and proxies",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.goodFor.0":
    "Explain why dataset count is an imperfect storage proxy",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.goodFor.1":
    "Show why the same number of rows can occupy different byte sizes",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.goodFor.2":
    "Separate a simple allowance metric from a measured resource quantity",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.intent":
    "Expose what an item count does not tell us about the amount of data.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.motionBeats.0":
    "Reveal two equal-count shelves.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.motionBeats.1":
    "Align persistent count marks.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.motionBeats.2":
    "Unfold exact byte strips on a common scale.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.motionBeats.3":
    "Reveal derived collection totals.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.motionBeats.4":
    "Hold count and measurement basis.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.motionBeats.5": "Shared opaque exit.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.name":
    "The same count can hold different amounts",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.notFor.0":
    "Exactly two equal-count groups and at most three items per group. Quantities are fictional measurement examples, not actual compression, transfer, memory, or storage benchmarks.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.notFor.1":
    "Every displayed total equals the sum of item bytes. Item count and byte volume remain distinct units; no conversion from count to bytes is inferred.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.notFor.2":
    "Both shelves use one zero, one scale, and one measurement basis. An empty-byte item keeps its count mark even though its size strip has zero length.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.notFor.3":
    "The selected datasets or rows grain applies to all items. A dataset and a row must never count as interchangeable units.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.notFor.4":
    "This does not assess whether a pricing policy is fair or predict actual costs. It illustrates a limitation of a proxy named in the strategy.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.notFor.5":
    "Supplied prose meaning, fictional status and agreement with structured choices are authoring responsibilities. Runtime validation enforces structure, numeric bounds, identities and references.",
  "motionAtlas.equal-count-unequal-volume.prompt":
    'Use Motion Atlas "The same count can hold different amounts" (equal-count-unequal-volume) as a conceptual graphic. Expose what an item count does not tell us about the amount of data. Replace fictional examples with approved authored content before making product claims.',
