  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.controls.unassigned": "unassigned",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.controls.unit": "unit",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.controls.value": "value",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.creativeDirection":
    "Reveal a neutral permission dock and a short arc of participant sockets. Seat the one token in the chosen holder's socket while all other sockets remain empty. A finite segmented collar around that socket drains in evenly spaced editorial beats; when it empties, the socket opens and the token retracts to the neutral dock. Hold the unassigned token and the prior holder's empty socket, making expiration different from a direct handoff, then fade to the opaque ground.",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.default.copy.dock": "Example permission pool",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.default.copy.example":
    "Fictional compressed timing",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.default.copy.expired": "Lease ended",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.default.copy.held": "Temporarily held",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.default.copy.unassigned":
    "Available, not assigned",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.default.lifetime.unit": "example turns",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.default.participants.0.label": "Example editor A",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.default.participants.1.label": "Example editor B",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.default.participants.2.label": "Example editor C",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.default.permissionLabel": "Example editing lease",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.description":
    "A single permission token temporarily occupies one participant's socket while its authored lifetime runs down. When the lease ends, the token returns to neutral custody before another participant can hold it.",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.distinction":
    "Custody-transfer moves responsibility after acceptance. This permission expires and returns to neutral custody with no successor, while a physically exclusive token makes its temporary nature visible. It is not an orbital ecosystem or a generic status cycle.",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.domains.0": "Editorial explanation",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.goodFor.0": "Explain a temporary edit lease",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.goodFor.1":
    "Illustrate a shared resource checked out for a limited period",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.goodFor.2":
    "Show permission returning to a pool after an authored expiry",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.intent":
    "Explain that temporary permission can end without transferring directly to another holder.",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.motionBeats.0":
    "Reveal the one held token and neutral dock.",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.motionBeats.1":
    "Drain one collar segment per evenly spaced authored beat.",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.motionBeats.2":
    "Release the expired socket and retract the token to neutral custody.",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.motionBeats.3":
    "Hold the unassigned token and empty previous socket.",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.name": "Borrowed Permission Returns",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.notFor.0":
    "There is always exactly one permission token. Socket count comes only from participants, and collar segment count comes only from lifetime.value.",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.notFor.1":
    "The six-second loop compresses the supplied lifetime and must not be interpreted as actual elapsed time or server-clock behavior.",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.notFor.2":
    "This illustrates an authored lease concept, not a verified distributed lock, fairness guarantee, race-condition solution, or automatic permission policy.",
  "motionAtlas.expiring-lease.prompt":
    "Explain that temporary permission can end without transferring directly to another holder.",
