  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.default.labels.original": "Original line",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.default.labels.removed":
    "Removed vertices",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.default.labels.simplified":
    "Simplified line",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.default.labels.unit": "grid units",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.description":
    "A schematic polyline shows all source vertices, then simplifies under a supplied perpendicular-distance tolerance. Removed vertices stay as ghosts with their deviation visible, while endpoints remain fixed.",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.distinction":
    "Unlike chart-focus-edit, actual geometry detail is reduced under a stated algorithmic tolerance. The original trace remains visible so simplification is inspectable.",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.domains.0": "Polyline simplification",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.goodFor.0":
    "Explain distance-tolerance polyline simplification",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.goodFor.1":
    "Show original geometry beside a reduced vertex trace",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.intent":
    "Make geometric simplification and its tolerance inspectable.",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.name":
    "Remove detail without moving the kept vertices",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.notFor.0":
    "This is an open-polyline teaching example, not topology-preserving polygon simplification.",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.notFor.1":
    "Douglas-Peucker is the explicit teaching algorithm; other simplifiers may produce different vertices.",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.notFor.2":
    "Tolerance is not GPS accuracy or evidence uncertainty.",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.notFor.3":
    "No live geography, online routing, JSX, functions, URLs, private records or external requests. Maps are schematic local plans; no real-world inference follows.",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.notFor.4":
    "Authored prose must identify schematic geography and accurately describe the selected example. Runtime validation preserves supplied prose and checks explicit structural and numeric rules without natural-language classification.",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.prompt":
    "React/SVG 960x600 canvas, shared palette, deterministic 180 frames at 30fps. This is schematic local geography with no real basemap. Frames 0-12 reveal. Frames 13-50 reveal a jagged source line and its vertices. Frames 51-110 run recursive farthest-deviation splits, retaining a vertex only when its deviation exceeds the tolerance. Frames 111-139 draw the simplified line over the ghost original and count retained/removed vertices. Hold at frames 140-165; fade to the same opaque ground at frames 166-179 for an editorial loop.",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.tags.0": "geometry simplification",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.tags.1": "Douglas-Peucker",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.tags.2": "vertex budget",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.tags.3": "distance tolerance",
  "motionAtlas.geometry-detail-budget.useWhen":
    "Make geometric simplification and its tolerance inspectable.",
