    "Reveal the authored setup.",
  "motionAtlas.habitat-corridor-reconnection.motionBeats.1":
    "Reveal habitat patches separated by working land and a road. At the land-management cue, lay the authored corridor footprint across the gap and lift its crossing over the road. Transfer that footprint's area from other land to habitat within the fixed boundary. Optionally move an explicitly illustrative marker along the supplied connection, then hold the conserved land balance.",
  "motionAtlas.habitat-corridor-reconnection.motionBeats.2":
    "Hold the resolved authored state and complete accounting.",
  "motionAtlas.habitat-corridor-reconnection.name":
    "Build a route between habitats",
  "motionAtlas.habitat-corridor-reconnection.notFor.0":
    "Total mapped area is conserved: existing habitat + other land before = existing habitat + corridor + other land after. The crossing is part of the corridor footprint, not additional habitat area.",
  "motionAtlas.habitat-corridor-reconnection.notFor.1":
    "Geometry is schematic; footprint area is calculated from supplied rectangular dimensions, while visual patch shape is not a geographic measurement.",
  "motionAtlas.habitat-corridor-reconnection.notFor.2":
    "Designed connectivity does not establish species suitability, movement, survival, biodiversity gain or long-term restoration success. Traversal is optional and explicitly illustrative; defaults are fictional.",
