  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.creativeDirection":
    "960x600 React/SVG with shared palette, deterministic 180 frames at 30fps. Reveal at frames 0-12. Frames 13-55 raise a small cone over each point. Frames 56-105 add cone heights into a sampled grid intensity. Frames 106-139 widen or narrow every cone to the second radius and recompute the grid while point markers stay fixed. Hold the resolved state at 140-165; fade to the same opaque ground at 166-179. Reset is editorial.",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.default.labels.intensity":
    "Illustrative intensity",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.default.labels.points":
    "Same point observations",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.default.labels.radius": "Smoothing radius",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.default.labels.unit": "kernel units",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.description":
    "Each supplied point contributes a bounded kernel to a schematic grid. The kernels add into one intensity field, then a second radius changes the smoothing without creating or deleting any point observations.",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.distinction":
    "Spatial-grid-binning assigns each point once to an exact count cell. This spreads each contribution across neighboring cells and makes radius a visible modeling choice.",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.domains.0": "Spatial smoothing",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.goodFor.0":
    "Explain how a heatmap radius changes smoothing",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.goodFor.1":
    "Distinguish modeled intensity from observed cell counts",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.intent":
    "Expose smoothing assumptions without presenting intensity as observed counts.",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.name":
    "A smooth surface depends on its radius",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.notFor.0":
    "This specified cone kernel is an instructional design, not a claim about a mapping library kernel.",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.notFor.1":
    "Intensity is neither case count, population, probability nor risk. Grid cell intensities do not sum to point count.",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.notFor.2":
    "A smooth field does not fill gaps in actual observations or establish conditions between points.",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.notFor.3":
    "No external requests, URLs, JSX or functions in props. Supplied examples are fictional.",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.notFor.4":
    "Authored prose remains the author’s responsibility. Runtime validation preserves supplied text without classifying its language or factual claims.",
  "motionAtlas.kernel-density-spread.prompt":
    "960x600 React/SVG with shared palette, deterministic 180 frames at 30fps. Reveal at frames 0-12. Frames 13-55 raise a small cone over each point. Frames 56-105 add cone heights into a sampled grid intensity. Frames 106-139 widen or narrow every cone to the second radius and recompute the grid while point markers stay fixed. Hold the resolved state at 140-165; fade to the same opaque ground at 166-179. Reset is editorial.",
