  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.controls.source.unit": "Unit",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.creativeDirection":
    "A source slider and two to four output rulers appear at their baseline positions. Visible mechanical couplings connect only outputs with nonzero multipliers. Over the middle two seconds the source slides to its trial setting and coupled pointers move simultaneously according to their supplied affine rules, with optional hollow baseline markers left behind. After a brief trial hold, the source slides back and every coupled pointer returns to its exact baseline. An uncoupled output stays still throughout. Hold the restored state with its authored caption, then fade to the same opaque ground within six seconds.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.default.contextLabel":
    "Fictional arithmetic example",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.default.outputs.0.label":
    "Demo parts",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.default.outputs.0.unit": "parts",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.default.outputs.1.label":
    "Demo reserve",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.default.outputs.1.unit": "credits",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.default.outputs.2.label":
    "Demo rooms",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.default.outputs.2.unit": "rooms",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.default.phaseLabels.baseline":
    "Starting assumption",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.default.phaseLabels.restored":
    "Starting values restored",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.default.phaseLabels.trial":
    "Try the alternative",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.default.source.label": "Demo batches",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.default.source.unit": "batches",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.description":
    "One source control moves to a trial value while explicitly coupled output scales respond. Returning the source restores every dependent value and leaves the independent example unchanged.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.distinction":
    "Unlike node-traversal or event-bus, no signal tours a graph. Physically coupled pointers move together under explicit equations, then reverse. Revision-restore replaces a saved document; this restores one source assumption and recomputes only its declared numeric dependents. Cell-normalization corrects values once, whereas these values remain linked throughout an intentional trial and return.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.domains.0": "Dependency mechanics",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.goodFor.0":
    "Explain which quantities change when a planning assumption changes",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.goodFor.1":
    "Demonstrate a reversible what-if calculation",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.goodFor.2":
    "Contrast a linked value with an explicitly independent constant",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.goodFor.3":
    "Rehearse a fictional per-user cost and allowance rule",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.goodFor.4":
    "Expose how one planning assumption changes only declared dependent quantities",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.intent":
    "Show the precise scope of a reversible change without implying every nearby quantity is affected.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.motionBeats.0":
    "Show baseline source and output pointers.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.motionBeats.1":
    "Move the source to trial and recompute each direct affine dependency.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.motionBeats.2":
    "Hold the trial values with independent outputs stationary.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.motionBeats.3":
    "Return to the exact baseline source and computed outputs.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.motionBeats.4":
    "Hold the restored values and caption.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.name": "Try a change, then return",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.notFor.0":
    "Only one source and direct affine dependencies are supported. No arbitrary graphs, cycles, chained expressions or inferred causal links.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.notFor.1":
    "Each output uses its own labeled fixed scale. Equal visual travel across rulers does not imply equal numerical change or comparable units.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.notFor.2":
    "Pointer positions always use multiplier times the current source plus offset, including intermediate frames. Fractions during movement are interpolation, not discrete operations performed.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.notFor.3":
    "Returning the parameter represents reversible arithmetic only. It does not claim that real-world impacts or external side effects can be undone.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.notFor.4":
    "Use the existing affine contract only. Tier cliffs, nonlinear growth, churn, caps, payment fees, and compounding require a separately specified model and must not be approximated silently.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.notFor.5":
    "A trial value is an authored scenario, not measured demand, market validation, or a prediction of financial performance. Use fictional values and explicit units and periods.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.notFor.6":
    "Affine calculations use IEEE-754 arithmetic. Overflowing products use half-scaled cancellation where the resulting value remains finite. Displayed and exported input values are not clamped.",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.prompt":
    'Use Motion Atlas "Try a change, then return" (linked-parameter-rehearsal) as a conceptual graphic. Show the precise scope of a reversible change without implying every nearby quantity is affected. Replace fictional sample content with approved authored content before making product claims.',
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.tags.0": "what if",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.tags.1": "sensitivity",
  "motionAtlas.linked-parameter-rehearsal.tags.10": "scenario assumptions",
