  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.description":
    "A field worker follows up a small, explicitly defined group whose visits were missed. A conversation, a booking, and an attended return resolve into separate outcomes.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.distinction":
    "Unlike status-cycle or node-traversal, this shows a worker contacting people in their physical setting and an actual return through a clinic doorway only for attended records. Unlike dose-cohort-return-paths, its denominator is a preselected missed-visit group and its action is reconnection.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.domains.0": "Human outreach and return",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.goodFor.0":
    "Explain the operational work after missed appointments.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.goodFor.1":
    "Distinguish successful contact from a booked or completed return.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.goodFor.2":
    "Show unresolved follow-up honestly in a fictional public health story.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.intent":
    "Show that reaching someone, booking a visit, and recording attendance are different achievements.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.motionBeats.0":
    "Establish the supplied identities and setting.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.motionBeats.1":
    "Frames 12..38 show four silhouettes with empty appointment marks beside their homes. Frames 39..114 animate one worker making the authored phone or doorstep contacts; a booking tab folds onto a calendar for one person, while only a documented attendee walks back through the clinic door. Frames 115..167 hold everyone in a distinct final state with the original group total; fade to ground by frame 179.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.motionBeats.2":
    "Hold the authored final records and derived quantities.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.motionBeats.3":
    "Return to the opaque ground through the shared envelope.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.name": "Reconnect after a missed visit",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.notFor.0":
    "The denominator is cases.length: the authored missed-visit group, not the whole service population. Each person has one exclusive final state, so state subtotals sum to the group total.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.notFor.1":
    "Attempts are contact events and may exceed unique people. A contact or booking does not imply attendance, vaccination, eligibility, or health benefit.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.notFor.2":
    "The sequence depicts recorded administrative outcomes and supplies no follow-up timing, clinical priority, or dosing advice.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.notFor.3":
    "Identities are fictional. Household and phone graphics must not imply a particular reason for the missed visit.",
  "motionAtlas.missed-visit-reconnect.prompt":
    "Use Reconnect after a missed visit (missed-visit-reconnect) for a fictional or approved authored example. Show that reaching someone, booking a visit, and recording attendance are different achievements.",
