  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.default.slots.2.label": "Slot C",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.default.slots.3.label": "Slot D",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.description":
    "A mobile clinic relocates between two schematic community sites, carrying a finite set of appointment slots. People receive only the explicitly assigned bookings, with open slots and unbooked people still visible.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.distinction":
    "Unlike radial-network or packet-stream, a physical service vehicle changes location and unfolds into a service point. Unlike outreach-household-revisits, the moving object is the service itself and the core constraint is one person per supplied slot, not visit activity.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.domains.0":
    "Mobile service and finite allocation",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.goodFor.0":
    "Explain a fictional mobile service relocation and bounded booking capacity.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.goodFor.1":
    "Show that moving a service and booking people are distinct from delivering care.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.goodFor.2":
    "Introduce community access planning while retaining unmet demand in the picture.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.intent":
    "Show a service moving toward a community while keeping finite appointment capacity and unbooked people visible.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.motionBeats.0":
    "Reveal the supplied setting and identities.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.motionBeats.1":
    "Frames 12..40 show a mobile clinic parked at the first site, nearby people, and its finite appointment-slot strip. Frames 41..113 fold the clinic awning, drive the same vehicle along a schematic road, and reopen it at the second site; assigned people connect to distinct slot tabs while unmatched people remain in place. Frames 114..167 hold both the person-booking ledger and slot-capacity ledger together; fade to ground by frame 179.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.motionBeats.2":
    "Hold the supplied final records and separate derived quantities.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.motionBeats.3":
    "Return to the opaque ground through the shared envelope.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.name": "Bring the service closer",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.notFor.0":
    "The people denominator is people.length. Booked people equals the number of non-null slotId values, and booked + unbooked equals the people total.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.notFor.1":
    "Slot capacity is slots.length. Occupied slots is the distinct assigned slotId count; occupied + open equals capacity. Each slot can have at most one assigned person, and no duplicated glyph creates extra capacity.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.notFor.2":
    "All assignments are authored. This is not a routing optimizer, access-distance model, clinical prioritization rule, eligibility decision, or recommendation for service placement.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.notFor.3":
    "Bookings are administrative plans, not attendance or treatment. The schematic map has no real geography, scale, journey time, distance measurement, or implied population coverage.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.prompt":
    "Use Bring the service closer (mobile-clinic-relocation) for a fictional or approved authored example. Show a service moving toward a community while keeping finite appointment capacity and unbooked people visible.",
  "motionAtlas.mobile-clinic-relocation.tags.0": "mobile clinic",
