    "showAuthorshipTab",
  "motionAtlas.peer-contribution-recognition.creativeDirection":
    "Frames 12..44 establish the contributor beside one or two authored work objects. Frames 45..88 let the colleague point to the focused object and trace its existing authorship tab back toward the contributor. Frames 89..128 turn the colleague toward the person and deliver the acknowledgment as a speech bubble or note. Frames 129..167 hold the contribution, authorship and acknowledgment together. If the authorship tab is hidden, keep the contributor's supplied name as a fixed byline beside the focused object instead. The colleague does not take the object or the credit. Use deterministic frame-driven React/SVG at 960x600, 180 frames and 30 fps, with the shared palette. Reveal during frames 0..11 and fade to the common opaque ground during frames 168..179.",
  "motionAtlas.peer-contribution-recognition.default.acknowledgment.text":
    "Your guide made the steps clear.",
  "motionAtlas.peer-contribution-recognition.default.contributions.0.label":
    "Clear setup guide",
