  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.default.metric.unit": "items",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.description":
    "A source table applies one explicit row predicate before selected record copies cross a transfer boundary. Excluded rows stay at the source and the destination displays exactly the transferred subset.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.distinction":
    "Unlike a generic data-pipeline, selection occurs before the boundary and only the matching rows are transferred. It differs from column-cache growth, which retains every row.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.domains.0": "Source-side filtering",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.goodFor.0":
    "Explain source-side row filtering before transfer",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.goodFor.1":
    "Show precisely which records a pushed predicate selects",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.intent":
    "Make the location of filtering relative to a transfer boundary explicit.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.motionBeats.0":
    "Reveal the schematic scene.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.motionBeats.1":
    "A source table applies one explicit row predicate before selected record copies cross a transfer boundary. Excluded rows stay at the source and the destination displays exactly the transferred subset.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.motionBeats.2":
    "Close source gates for nonmatching rows.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.motionBeats.3":
    "Move only matching row copies across the boundary while retaining all originals.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.motionBeats.4":
    "Hold the complete resolved relationship.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.motionBeats.5":
    "The outer stock envelope fades to the same opaque ground.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.name":
    "Apply the row condition before transfer",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.notFor.0":
    "The source is assumed to support this predicate; source capabilities must be established before presenting a real implementation claim.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.notFor.1":
    "Rows are not bytes: fewer rows does not establish a measured bandwidth reduction.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.notFor.2":
    "Predicate correctness and source capability are supplied assumptions.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.notFor.3":
    "No JSX, functions, URLs or external fetch in props. The animation is an authored explanation, not actual document extraction or product evidence.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.notFor.4":
    "Authored prose and schematic context are the author's responsibility. Runtime validation checks structural bounds and numeric, reference and geometry constraints, without classifying natural-language claims.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.notFor.5":
    "Source IDs preserve exact authored characters, including empty strings. Whitespace uses distinct literal-data marks.",
  "motionAtlas.predicate-pushdown-boundary.prompt":
    "Use Motion Atlas Apply the row condition before transfer (predicate-pushdown-boundary) to make the location of filtering relative to a transfer boundary explicit. Supply approved authored content before making claims.",
