  "motionAtlas.protected-work-boundary.description":
    "A worker declines to squeeze a new request into a protected time block. The request moves to a visible deferred tray, or to an explicitly available work block, while the schedule retains its original size.",
  "motionAtlas.protected-work-boundary.distinction":
    "Unlike schedule-buffer, no interruption consumes reserve time. Unlike person-led-support-calendar, the central decision can leave work deliberately unscheduled, preserving a finite workload boundary instead of finding a new appointment.",
