    "Copy selected values and headings into a separate revision-labeled snapshot.",
  "motionAtlas.publication-snapshot-slice.motionBeats.3":
    "Fade the old live value and write the authored edit only in its live cell. Keep published values, audience and revision frozen. The outer renderer fades at 166..179.",
  "motionAtlas.publication-snapshot-slice.name":
    "Freeze the selected data for a published view",
  "motionAtlas.publication-snapshot-slice.notFor.0":
    "No publishing action is performed. Internal and public are authored audience labels, not implemented access control.",
  "motionAtlas.publication-snapshot-slice.notFor.1":
    "A frozen snapshot can become outdated; it must retain its revision.",
  "motionAtlas.publication-snapshot-slice.notFor.2":
    "Selected data may still be sensitive; selection alone is no anonymization guarantee.",
  "motionAtlas.publication-snapshot-slice.notFor.3":
    "No JSX, functions, URLs or external fetch in props. The animation is an authored explanation, not actual document extraction or product evidence.",
  "motionAtlas.publication-snapshot-slice.notFor.4":
    "Column and row IDs are exact unique strings with maximum length 18, no minimum. Each source row cells length equals columns length. Selection rowIds/columnIds are nonempty unique subsets of existing source IDs; empty references are valid when an empty target ID exists. Live edit references a selected existing source cell and differs exactly from its pre-edit value. Snapshot cells equal selected rows times selected columns, in selection order, retaining pre-edit values and revision. Audience is explicit and never inferred.",
  "motionAtlas.publication-snapshot-slice.notFor.5":
    "Prose meaning is an author responsibility. Runtime validation enforces structural bounds, exact references and numeric/geometric rules.",
  "motionAtlas.publication-snapshot-slice.prompt":
    'Use Motion Atlas "Freeze the selected data for a published view" (publication-snapshot-slice) as an authored conceptual explanation. Separate live data from a bounded frozen publication. Supply approved content before making product claims.',
