    "Make the edges precise",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.default.statements.1.context":
    "Final fictional diagram",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.description":
    "Two apparently conflicting statements first face each other, then separate into explicit contexts that explain how both can apply. The qualifier is supplied by the author and stays visible in the final arrangement.",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.distinction":
    "Unlike paired-contrast, this begins with apparent incompatibility and resolves it by revealing distinct scopes of truth. The semantic transformation is qualification rather than comparison or choosing a winner.",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.domains.0":
    "Tradeoffs and qualifications",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.goodFor.0":
    "Resolve an apparent contradiction by naming context",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.goodFor.1":
    "Distinguish a generalization from a situation-specific statement",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.goodFor.2":
    "Explain why advice changes under different conditions",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.goodFor.3":
    "Separate source-code availability from access to independently curated content",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.goodFor.4":
    "Clarify that price sensitivity and willingness to pay are different statements",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.goodFor.5":
    "Separate the time spent preparing from the time needed for a later response",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.intent":
    "Explain how two statements can coexist when their contexts differ.",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.motionBeats.0":
    "Establish the authored starting arrangement.",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.motionBeats.1":
    "Two short claims enter on opposing horizontal tracks and stop at a central question mark. A context divider unfolds vertically, moving each claim to its own labeled region. The question mark resolves into a small joining brace with the authored qualifier below it. Both context-claim pairs hold together before the shared fade, without rewriting either claim.",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.motionBeats.2":
    "Hold the resolved authored relationships before the shared exit.",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.name": "Both can be true",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.notFor.0":
    "The author must provide a valid contextual reconciliation; the renderer cannot establish that both claims are true.",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.notFor.1":
    "Exactly two claims are shown, each with one context.",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.notFor.2":
    "The graphic must not be used to hide a genuine unresolved contradiction behind decorative separation.",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.notFor.3":
    "Show only supplied policy statements and their distinct objects. The animation does not interpret licenses, determine ownership, confer rights, or prove that any legal position is correct.",
  "motionAtlas.qualify-apparent-conflict.notFor.4":
    "A low price, paid plan, or free offer by itself proves neither high nor low technical quality.",
