    "Read names",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.default.requests.1.label":
    "Read items",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.description":
    "A cached table answers a narrower column request, then grows to include newly requested columns. Every original row remains in the same order and only one live cache entry remains.",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.distinction":
    "Cache-reuse compares identical keys. This changes the needed set, tests containment, and replaces one narrower relation with a wider relation without joining fragments.",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.domains.0": "Editorial illustration",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.goodFor.0":
    "Explain why a subset cache hit can become a wider-query miss",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.goodFor.1":
    "Show column projection that preserves duplicate source rows",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.intent":
    "Explain exact column coverage and monotone cache growth without changing row grain.",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.motionBeats.0":
    "Match the covered request against the cache.",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.motionBeats.1":
    "Expose missing columns for the second request.",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.motionBeats.2":
    "Widen one cache while preserving every row occurrence.",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.motionBeats.3":
    "Hold the complete union of columns.",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.name":
    "Widen the cache without losing rows",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.notFor.0":
    "Projection removes columns only. Duplicate rows and physical row order must not change.",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.notFor.1":
    "The origin may still deliver every column; drawn cache savings do not imply network pushdown.",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.notFor.2":
    "Freshness, authorization and source version changes are not modeled.",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.notFor.3":
    "No real product screen, external fetch, supplied code execution, or measured performance claim. All text is authored; no JSX, functions or URLs in props.",
  "motionAtlas.query-column-cache-growth.notFor.4":
    "Supplied prose is preserved. Fictional framing, evidence, and agreement between wording and selected states are authoring responsibilities. Runtime validation enforces structural bounds and explicit cross-field rules.",
