  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.creativeDirection":
    "Frames 12..38 reveal a schematic pipe joint leaking beside its normal outlet. Frames 39..62 place a catch tray under the leak while flow continues through the joint. Frames 63..106 pause the flow and let the worker apply the authored joint repair. Frames 107..140 restore the normal outlet flow only when a retest exists, showing either no side leak or a continued side leak according to the supplied result. For not-tested, retain the paused flow and an untested tag. Frames 141..167 hold the catch tray, repaired joint and explicit observation. The normal outlet must still run for a stopped-leak result so closing the supply cannot masquerade as prevention. Use deterministic frame-driven React/SVG at 960x600, 180 frames and 30 fps, with the shared palette. Reveal during frames 0..11 and fade to the common opaque ground during frames 168..179.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.default.fixtureLabel":
    "Illustrative joint",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.default.labels.containment":
    "Temporary containment",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.default.labels.continued":
    "Leak still observed",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.default.labels.example":
    "Fictional system metaphor",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.default.labels.repair":
    "Source repair",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.default.labels.stopped":
    "No leak observed",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.default.labels.test":
    "Illustrated retest",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.default.labels.untested":
    "Not retested",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.default.repair.label":
    "Replace the joint seal",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.default.workerLabel":
    "Maintenance partner",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.description":
    "A worker first contains a recurring leak, then repairs its source and performs one supplied retest. Temporary containment and prevention remain visibly different actions.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.distinction":
    "Unlike grievance-remedy-retest, this explicitly separates downstream containment from upstream intervention and checks recurrence under resumed operation. Unlike retry-backoff, the underlying object changes before the retry.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.domains.0": "Editorial illustration",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.goodFor.0":
    "Distinguish immediate relief from recurring-cause repair",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.goodFor.1":
    "Explain incident follow-through without celebrating constant crisis",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.goodFor.2":
    "Retain a failed or unperformed retest",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.intent":
    "Make source repair visibly different from repeatedly managing its consequences.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.motionBeats.0":
    "Reveal a leaking joint beside its running normal outlet.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.motionBeats.1":
    "Place a catch tray under the side leak without stopping flow.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.motionBeats.2":
    "Pause flow while the worker applies the authored joint repair.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.motionBeats.3":
    "Resume flow only for a supplied retest and retain its actual result.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.motionBeats.4":
    "Hold the tray, repaired joint and explicit observation.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.name":
    "Fix the source after containing the leak",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.notFor.0":
    "This is a schematic operational metaphor, not a plumbing tutorial or a diagnosis of a real incident.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.notFor.1":
    "Drops and line thickness are nonquantitative motion cues. No volume, loss rate or saved cost is claimed.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.notFor.2":
    "One authored observation cannot establish permanent prevention. A repair action alone never determines the test outcome.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.notFor.3":
    "Supplied prose is preserved. Fictional framing, evidence and agreement between wording and selected states are authoring responsibilities. Runtime validation enforces structural bounds and explicit cross-field rules.",
  "motionAtlas.recurring-leak-prevention.prompt":
    "Make source repair visibly different from repeatedly managing its consequences.",
