  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.creativeDirection":
    "Frames 12..40 reveal an artifact with its authored issue tabs and an empty repair register. Frames 41..90 unfold each open follow-up tab into a matching register entry with its owner and due label, leaving the original limitation attached to the artifact. Resolved issues keep a resolved mark. Frames 91..130 move the artifact to the recipient only if every blocking issue is resolved. Otherwise keep it behind a held bracket. Frames 131..167 hold the actual artifact location and all unresolved obligations. A due label is a commitment, never a completed repair. Use deterministic frame-driven React/SVG at 960x600, 180 frames and 30 fps, with the shared palette. Reveal during frames 0..11 and fade to the common opaque ground during frames 168..179.",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.default.artifact.label":
    "Workshop guide",
