  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.default.labels.ready":
    "Ready to share",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.default.labels.register":
    "Repair commitments",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.default.labels.resolved": "Resolved",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.default.recipientLabel":
    "Workshop team",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.description":
    "An artifact may move to a recipient only when no open blocking issue remains. Every open follow-up issue stays attached as a visible limitation and creates an owned, dated repair obligation.",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.distinction":
    "Unlike readiness-latch, the result may move while explicitly classified follow-up obligations remain open. Unlike feedback-refinement, delivery does not imply a finished revision cycle; unresolved work retains identity, an owner and a due label.",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.domains.0": "Editorial illustration",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.goodFor.0":
    "Explain a bounded release without erasing known limitations",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.goodFor.1":
    "Keep technical debt ownership visible after delivery",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.goodFor.2":
    "Distinguish an open blocker from an explicitly deferred follow-up",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.intent":
    "Separate delivery from the continuing duty to address known flaws.",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.motionBeats.0":
    "Reveal the artifact, attached issue marks and empty repair register.",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.motionBeats.1":
    "Unfold every open follow-up into its owned, dated register entry.",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.motionBeats.2":
    "Deliver only when no open blocker remains.",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.motionBeats.3":
    "Hold the actual location with every open limitation and obligation.",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.name":
    "Deliver with the remaining repair obligations visible",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.notFor.0":
    "Issue severity and release acceptability are authored, never inferred from text. The renderer cannot decide whether a flaw is safe.",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.notFor.1":
    "Do not use the generic example to justify releasing software with dangerous or unknown consequences.",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.notFor.2":
    "The register proves only that a commitment was stated. It does not show or guarantee that a later repair occurs.",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.notFor.3":
    "Supplied prose is preserved. Fictional framing, evidence and agreement between wording and selected states are authoring responsibilities. Runtime validation enforces structural bounds and explicit cross-field rules.",
  "motionAtlas.release-repair-obligations.prompt":
    "Separate delivery from the continuing duty to address known flaws.",
