    "Reveal one learner at a classroom desk with the supplied prior-work samples, preserving their authored forms and marks without grading them. Move the learner and the same portfolio to a side table while the interruption-period label appears. Bring the learner back to the desk, where the teacher places exactly the supplied return activities. Link each review activity to its referenced prior work and show each new activity without inventing a prior artifact. Hold the original work and supplied activities together, then fade out.",
