  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.controls.reserveUnits.help":
    "Initial unused duration between the last task and the deadline. Integer 1..4; deadline position is derived from task durations plus this reserve",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.controls.resultLabel": "resultLabel",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.controls.resultLabel.help":
    "States the authored result above the resolved schedule. 1..38 characters",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.controls.scheduleLabels": "scheduleLabels",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.controls.scheduleLabels.help":
    "Names the flexible reserve segment and the fixed endpoint. Both keys required; each label 1..20 characters",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.controls.showValues": "showValues",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.controls.showValues.help":
    "Shows authored durations and the derived remaining reserve next to their segments. boolean",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.controls.tasks": "tasks",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.controls.tasks.help":
    "The sequential task blocks, their order, and their shared-unit durations. 2..4 tasks; unique IDs <= 16 characters; labels 1..16 characters; integer durations 1..4",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.controls.unitLabel": "unitLabel",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.controls.unitLabel.help":
    "Names the common unit for tasks, delay, and reserve. 1..12 characters; all durations share this unit",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.creativeDirection":
    "During 12..44, assemble one horizontal schedule from proportionally sized task blocks followed by a hatched reserve segment and a stationary deadline pin. During 44..74, reveal the supplied interruption block immediately after its named task. During 74..118, the remaining task blocks translate together by the interruption's width and the reserve shortens by exactly that width. A contour along the schedule keeps the total endpoint aligned with the unchanged deadline pin. Hold the inserted interruption, shifted tasks, and remaining reserve through 168, then exit to the opaque ground. The viewer sees precisely where the delay was absorbed.",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.default.interruption.label": "Extra pass",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.default.resultLabel":
    "Reserve absorbs the delay",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.default.scheduleLabels.deadline": "Delivery",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.default.scheduleLabels.reserve": "Reserve",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.default.tasks.0.label": "Draft",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.default.tasks.1.label": "Review",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.default.tasks.2.label": "Send",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.default.unitLabel": "slots",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.description":
    "A scheduled sequence leaves a visible reserve before a fixed deadline. An interruption shifts later work into that reserve while the deadline stays in place.",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.distinction":
    "This conserves one schedule's total width while reallocating reserve time. It is neither a chart of changing rankings nor a pipeline whose stages merely activate in order.",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.domains.0": "Editorial explanation",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.goodFor.0":
    "Explaining planned slack in a schedule",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.goodFor.1":
    "Showing a bounded delay absorbed before a deadline",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.goodFor.2":
    "Discussing contingency without changing the scope of the planned work",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.intent":
    "Show how unused schedule capacity can absorb a specific interruption.",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.motionBeats.0":
    "Assemble proportional tasks, reserve, and a fixed deadline.",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.motionBeats.1":
    "Reveal the interruption after its named task.",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.motionBeats.2":
    "Translate later tasks and consume exactly the delay width.",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.motionBeats.3":
    "Hold the conserved schedule and remaining reserve.",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.name": "Let the buffer absorb a delay",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.notFor.0":
    "The default schedule is fictional; segment widths exactly encode supplied duration units, not evidence of real delivery performance.",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.notFor.1":
    "The interruption must fit within the supplied reserve; overruns and moving deadlines are intentionally excluded.",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.notFor.2":
    "Tasks are sequential, indivisible, and unchanged in duration; parallel work and resource calendars are not modeled.",
  "motionAtlas.schedule-buffer.prompt":
    "Show how unused schedule capacity can absorb a specific interruption.",
