    "Keeps the before and expanded captions beside the corresponding header outlines. boolean; hiding captions cannot remove missing-value marks or the later-record distinction",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.controls.showVersionLabels.label":
    "Show version labels",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.creativeDirection":
    "On a 960x600 React/SVG canvas, frames 0-11 reveal a compact table of earlier records. Frames 12-48 slide the existing columns left and unfold one new column from the header seam. Frames 49-92 place an explicit not-collected mark in that column for each earlier record without changing any original value. Frames 93-132 seat one later record in the same table, with its authored new-field value or missing mark. Frames 133-167 hold both generations under the new header and optional version captions. Frames 168-179 fade to the shared opaque palette ground, giving a deterministic six-second loop at 30fps.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.earlierRecords.0.label":
    "Demo record A",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.earlierRecords.0.recordedValue":
    "North",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.earlierRecords.1.label":
    "Demo record B",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.earlierRecords.1.recordedValue":
    "South",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.evidenceLabel":
    "Fictional records; no historical backfill",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.fields.addedLabel": "Visit mode",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.fields.existingLabel": "Site",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.fields.missingLabel":
    "Not collected",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.laterRecord.addedValue":
    "In person",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.laterRecord.label":
    "Demo record C",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.laterRecord.recordedValue":
    "East",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.phaseLabels.before":
    "Earlier collection",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.phaseLabels.expanded":
    "One question added",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.default.phaseLabels.later":
    "Later record arrives",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.description":
    "A small table gains one new field while every earlier record keeps its identity and its uncollected value. A later record supplies a value under the expanded schema, leaving the older gaps visible.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.distinction":
    "Unlike cell-normalization, this changes the available field structure without correcting existing values. Unlike schema-mapping, no fields are paired across two schemas. Unlike state-preserving-source-refresh, the visible change is a new collection question and its historical absence, not refreshing values from an existing source.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.domains.0":
    "Schema change and retained evidence",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.goodFor.0":
    "Explain an evolving collection form during a changing field program",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.goodFor.1":
    "Show why adding a question does not supply historical answers",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.goodFor.2":
    "Introduce a schema extension before discussing any backfill process",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.intent":
    "Separate the addition of a field from the collection of a value for that field.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.motionBeats.0": "Reveal earlier rows.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.motionBeats.1":
    "Unfold the added header from its seam.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.motionBeats.2":
    "Mark historical values as not collected.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.motionBeats.3":
    "Seat the supplied later record.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.motionBeats.4": "Hold both generations.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.motionBeats.5": "Shared opaque exit.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.name":
    "Add a field without inventing the past",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.notFor.0":
    "One retained field, one added field, one later row, and at most three earlier rows fit the six-second explanation.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.notFor.1":
    "The ending record count is earlierRecords.length + 1. A new column does not create or remove earlier records.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.notFor.2":
    "The earlier records always retain missing marks in the added column. No default, imputation, migration, enrichment, or retrospectively inferred answer is shown.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.notFor.3":
    "The sequence is a conceptual collection example. It makes no claim about a particular database migration system or any shipped form-editing feature.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.notFor.4":
    "The editorial fade resets the illustration, not the stored records. All labels are supplied inputs.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.notFor.5":
    "Supplied prose meaning, fictional status and agreement with structured choices are authoring responsibilities. Runtime validation enforces structure, numeric bounds, identities and references.",
  "motionAtlas.schema-column-evolution.prompt":
    'Use Motion Atlas "Add a field without inventing the past" (schema-column-evolution) as a conceptual graphic. Separate the addition of a field from the collection of a value for that field. Replace fictional examples with approved authored content before making product claims.',
