  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.creativeDirection":
    "A broad heading and a flat field of topic labels appear together. A rectangular aperture draws around the full field, then its edges contract and selected labels slide together within it while other labels remain outside. The narrowed question replaces the broad heading inside the frame. A final outside caption clarifies what is deferred before the common exit envelope.",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.default.broadTopic":
    "Planning a fictional studio",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.default.focusedQuestion":
    "Where will supplies be stored?",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.default.insideLabel": "This explanation",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.default.outsideLabel": "Other topics come later",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.default.topics.0.label": "Lighting",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.default.topics.1.label": "Storage shelves",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.default.topics.2.label": "Supply bins",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.default.topics.3.label": "Seating",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.description":
    "A broad subject remains visible while a movable frame isolates the subset under discussion. Excluded topics stay outside the frame with explicit context rather than disappearing without explanation.",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.distinction":
    "The explanatory action is a changing semantic boundary with explicit membership. Unlike stagger-cards or word-reveal, the labels begin visible and the animation changes which topics belong to the current question.",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.domains.0": "Editorial connectors",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.goodFor.0": "Define what an explainer will cover",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.goodFor.1":
    "Move from a broad subject to one bounded question",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.goodFor.2":
    "Separate current scope from deferred topics",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.goodFor.3":
    "Separate a long-term lifecycle vision from a bounded present focus",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.goodFor.4":
    "Clarify the domain and tasks an example is intended to cover",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.intent":
    "Make the boundary of the current explanation explicit.",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.motionBeats.0":
    "Establish the authored starting arrangement.",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.motionBeats.1":
    "A broad heading and a flat field of topic labels appear together. A rectangular aperture draws around the full field, then its edges contract and selected labels slide together within it while other labels remain outside. The narrowed question replaces the broad heading inside the frame. A final outside caption clarifies what is deferred before the common exit envelope.",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.motionBeats.2":
    "Hold the resolved authored relationships before the shared exit.",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.name": "Narrow the question",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.notFor.0":
    "The frame expresses topic membership, not physical geography or measured area.",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.notFor.1":
    "Included topics are authored; the renderer performs no text classification.",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.notFor.2":
    "This is a single narrowing step, not an animated camera zoom through a hierarchy.",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.notFor.3":
    "Topics outside the aperture may be future, deferred, unsupported, or simply out of this explanation. Supply the correct outside label and do not imply they are shipped features.",
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.prompt":
    'Use Motion Atlas "Narrow the question" (scope-aperture) as a conceptual graphic. Make the boundary of the current explanation explicit. Replace fictional sample content with approved authored content before making product claims.',
  "motionAtlas.scope-aperture.tags.0": "scope",
