    "Author whether the recipient opens the envelope or whether the loop ends with it sealed.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.controls.showExteriorReference":
    "showExteriorReference",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.controls.showExteriorReference.help":
    "Show the supplied reference on the exterior while sender and recipient remain available.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.controls.showLabels": "showLabels",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.controls.showLabels.help":
    "Show the supplied address, brief text, and captions.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.creativeDirection":
    "Begin with a short open brief resting over an unfolded envelope. Fold the lower and side flaps over the brief, then lower the final flap so the contents are fully occluded rather than faded. Move the closed envelope along one shallow hand-carried arc to a recipient tray. If the configured reveal rule is recipient, peel the flap open only after the envelope settles; otherwise hold it sealed. Resolve on the authored final state before the seam-safe fade.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.default.address.recipient": "Example coordinator",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.default.address.reference": "Example brief A",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.default.address.sender": "Example author",
