    "Example meeting: blue shed",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.default.brief.1.line":
    "Example topic: crate labels",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.default.copy.contents": "Example brief contents",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.default.copy.covered": "Contents covered",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.default.copy.example":
    "Fictional physical metaphor",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.default.copy.opened": "Opened by recipient",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.default.copy.received": "Received, still sealed",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.description":
    "An open brief folds into an opaque envelope, moves to its named recipient, and opens only at the authored reveal point. The address remains visible while the contents are covered.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.distinction":
    "This is a fold, opaque enclosure, and recipient-controlled reveal, unlike packet-stream's visible abstract packets. It covers the complete payload rather than the field subset selection in disclosure-aperture.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.domains.0": "Concealment and reveal",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.goodFor.0":
    "Distinguish visible routing information from covered contents",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.goodFor.1":
    "Explain a confidential briefing metaphor",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.goodFor.2":
    "Introduce a restricted handoff before separately documenting the actual security mechanism",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.intent":
    "Show that routing a package and revealing its contents are separate actions.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.motionBeats.0":
    "Both reveal modes begin with the readable open brief.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.motionBeats.1":
    "Lower, side and final flaps enclose the brief opaquely.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.motionBeats.2":
    "The covered brief travels to the recipient tray.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.motionBeats.3":
    "Only recipient mode opens after arrival. Remain-sealed keeps the cover closed.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.name": "The Contents Stay Covered",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.notFor.0":
    "A sealed-envelope metaphor is not proof of encryption, identity verification, authorization, secure deletion, or protection from any particular adversary.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.notFor.1":
    "Exterior address and reference are deliberately visible. Do not describe the depiction as hiding all metadata.",
  "motionAtlas.sealed-handoff.notFor.2":
    "The brief contains exactly the supplied lines and does not represent a measured payload size.",
