    "Receipts minor",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.controls.showAmounts": "Show amounts",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.creativeDirection":
    "Frames 0-11 reveal two equal-sized period trays and one common monetary ruler on the 960x600 canvas. Frames 12-65 partition the first receipt strip into operating outflow, temporary distribution, and retained cash. Frames 66-95 turn the authored term marker between the trays and close only the temporary-distribution outlet. Frames 96-140 lay the second identical receipt strip into the second tray: operating outflow stays the same and the formerly distributed portion remains in retained cash. Frames 141-167 hold both periods and their exact reconciliation side by side. Exit to shared opaque ground at frames 168-179. Use frame-driven React/SVG at 30fps and no stochastic timing.",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.default.arrangement.label":
    "Demo temporary distribution",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.default.arrangement.termBoundaryLabel":
    "Authored term ends",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.default.copy.distribution":
    "Temporary distribution",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.default.copy.example":
    "Fictional arithmetic; no financial forecast",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.default.copy.operating":
    "Operating outflow",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.default.copy.receipts":
    "Period receipts",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.default.copy.retained":
    "Retained period cash",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.default.money.unitLabel":
    "demo credits",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.default.periods.0.label":
    "Demo period A",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.default.periods.1.label":
    "Demo period B",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.description":
    "Two equal-length fictional receipt periods expose the same operating outflow and a temporary distribution. After the authored term boundary, that distribution no longer leaves and the retained period cash increases by the exact amount, without forecasting growth or solvency.",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.distinction":
    "Unlike pooled-donor-allocation, the explanation compares two separate time-bounded receipt flows after a term changes. Unlike expiring-lease, no exclusive permission token returns to neutral custody. The expired outlet changes one conserved cash partition while equal receipts and operating outflow expose its exact effect.",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.domains.0":
    "Time-bounded resource accounting",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.goodFor.0":
    "Explain the arithmetic of a temporary distribution ending",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.goodFor.1":
    "Separate cash received, operating outflow, distributions, and retained period cash",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.goodFor.2":
    "Show a bounded financing tradeoff without projecting company performance",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.intent":
    "Make the effect of ending one temporary cash distribution inspectable while other quantities remain fixed.",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.name": "When a temporary share ends",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.notFor.0":
    "This is an illustrative arithmetic model, not financial advice, investment terms, a valuation, a profit statement, or a solvency projection. It uses no company financial figures.",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.notFor.1":
    "Each period reconciles receipts = operating outflow + active distribution + retained period cash. The second retained amount exceeds the first by the first distribution, with all other inputs fixed.",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.notFor.2":
    "Compute the active distribution using integer basis-point arithmetic. Reject fractional minor-unit distributions or negative retained amounts.",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.notFor.3":
    "Both periods are separate flows over equal durations. Do not carry the first remainder into the second tray or display their sum as a company balance.",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.notFor.4":
    "Operating outflow is a supplied composite. Taxes, financing transactions, accruals, other liabilities, ownership, and legal treatment are outside the model. No claim about employee compensation or investor rights follows from the illustration.",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.notFor.5":
    "Free prose is author supplied; only structural, reference, numeric and documented lexical constraints are runtime-validated.",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.prompt":
    "Two equal-length fictional receipt periods expose the same operating outflow and a temporary distribution. After the authored term boundary, that distribution no longer leaves and the retained period cash increases by the exact amount, without forecasting growth or solvency.",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.tags.0": "temporary revenue share",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.tags.1": "term boundary",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.tags.2": "cash allocation",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.tags.3": "retained cash",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.tags.4": "resource accounting",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.tags.5": "distribution expiry",
  "motionAtlas.term-limited-revenue-share.useWhen":
    "Make the effect of ending one temporary cash distribution inspectable while other quantities remain fixed.",
