  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.creativeDirection":
    "A slim vertical hinge appears beneath the approach label. Its left leaf unfolds to show the gained qualities, then the hinge pivots just enough to reveal the right leaf with the concessions. Both settle open at equal readable size, and a short priority statement locks beneath the hinge as the final hold. The angle is fixed editorial motion rather than a numeric balance.",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.default.approach": "A fictional pocket notebook",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.default.concessions.0.label":
    "Less room for large sketches",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.default.gains.0.label": "Fits in a small bag",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.default.gains.1.label": "Easy to open anywhere",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.default.priorityStatement":
    "For this example, portability comes first",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.default.sideLabels.concession": "What we give up",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.default.sideLabels.gain": "What we gain",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.description":
    "A selected approach rotates into view with a benefit on one face and a concession on the other. Both faces open into a single hinge so the final choice retains its tradeoff.",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.distinction":
    "A single hinged argument exposes an inseparable benefit and concession. It does not rank alternatives like bar-race or merely reveal a sibling collection like stagger-cards.",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.domains.0": "Tradeoffs and qualifications",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.goodFor.0":
    "Explain a choice that gains one property at another's expense",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.goodFor.1":
    "State the downside alongside an advantage",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.goodFor.2":
    "Make a design rationale honest about its constraints",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.goodFor.3":
    "Explain a relationship-intensive service choice with its time requirement",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.goodFor.4":
    "Keep a mission constraint visible alongside a growth opportunity",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.intent":
    "Keep a chosen approach's benefit and concession visible together.",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.motionBeats.0":
    "The labeled setup establishes the authored comparison.",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.motionBeats.1":
    "A slim vertical hinge appears beneath the approach label. Its left leaf unfolds to show the gained qualities, then the hinge pivots just enough to reveal the right leaf with the concessions. Both settle open at equal readable size, and a short priority statement locks beneath the hinge as the final hold. The angle is fixed editorial motion rather than a numeric balance.",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.motionBeats.2":
    "Both sides remain readable in the resolved hold.",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.name": "A choice has two sides",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.notFor.0":
    "The number of listed points is not a score and cannot establish which side outweighs the other.",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.notFor.1":
    "Leaf sizes and hinge angles carry no quantitative meaning.",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.notFor.2":
    "No conclusion is calculated; the priority statement must be authored and qualified for its context.",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.notFor.3":
    "A stated strategic preference does not establish investor duties, future behavior, customer conversion, financial return, or moral superiority. Keep the authored context and concession visible.",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.options.concession-first": "concession-first",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.options.gain-first": "gain-first",
  "motionAtlas.tradeoff-pivot.prompt":
    'Use Motion Atlas "A choice has two sides" (tradeoff-pivot) as a conceptual graphic. Keep a chosen approach\'s benefit and concession visible together. Keep the restrained motion and readable labels; replace sample content with approved facts before making product claims.',
