  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.controls.reference.value": "Value",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.controls.showValues": "Show values",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.creativeDirection":
    "At the entrance, a supplied estimate marker stands on a fixed ruler. Two folded sleeves extend from the marker to the supplied lower and upper endpoints, exposing a patterned interval and its explicit meaning. An optional reference blade then lowers across the ruler, with its position preserved even when it crosses the interval. Hold the estimate, both endpoints, interval label and authored interpretation together before fading to the opaque ground. All movement fits six seconds and reveals supplied values rather than simulating evidence or a time trend.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.default.axis.unit": "hours",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.default.contextLabel":
    "Fictional planning example",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.default.estimate.label":
    "Demo preparation time",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.default.interpretation":
    "The range spans the planning allowance.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.default.interval.label":
    "Illustrative planning range",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.default.reference.label":
    "Demo planning allowance",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.description":
    "A point estimate opens into a bounded interval on one fixed scale. An optional reference remains visible so the interval's relation to that reference can be read without turning uncertainty into certainty.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.distinction":
    "Unlike line-trace, the scale has no time axis and no observed series is drawn. Unlike chart-focus-edit, this reveals the uncertainty contract hidden by a point alone. Contact-window-overlap compares recorded visits in time; this unfolds one numerical estimate into its explicitly named epistemic bounds.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.domains.0": "Quantitative explanation",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.goodFor.0":
    "Explain why a single planning estimate has a range",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.goodFor.1":
    "Introduce a supplied confidence interval alongside its point estimate",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.goodFor.2":
    "Show that a reference value lies within or outside authored bounds",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.goodFor.3":
    "Label a supplied scenario range separately from statistical uncertainty",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.goodFor.4":
    "Keep an untested operating assumption visible beside a point estimate",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.intent":
    "Make the limits around an estimate as visible as the estimate itself.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.motionBeats.0":
    "Establish the estimate on the fixed ruler.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.motionBeats.1":
    "Unfold the two interval sleeves to their supplied endpoints.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.motionBeats.2":
    "Lower the optional reference at its fixed value.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.motionBeats.3":
    "Hold the bounds, point and authored interpretation.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.name": "Show the range behind the estimate",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.notFor.0":
    "One estimate and at most one reference. Endpoints are supplied, never statistically calculated or narrowed by the animation.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.notFor.1":
    "Interval width represents numeric span on a linear scale, not probability density, likelihood or sample size.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.notFor.2":
    "Confidence intervals, measurement ranges and scenario ranges are different meanings. The selected kind and label must match the source.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.notFor.3":
    "Crossing or not crossing a reference is not automatically a significance test, recommendation or certainty claim. No automatic success or failure color is applied.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.notFor.4":
    "A conservative adjustment or downside scenario is not a confidence interval, a validated error margin, or a representative population estimate. Match interval.kind and its visible label to the actual evidence.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.notFor.5":
    "No endpoints, probabilities, sample precision, or validation status are inferred from a business plan or the width of the displayed band.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.notFor.6":
    "Endpoint values use external slots and leader lines so coincident point and endpoint positions remain readable. Finite extreme spans use stable normalization without changing the axis.",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.prompt":
    'Use Motion Atlas "Show the range behind the estimate" (uncertainty-unfold) as a conceptual graphic. Make the limits around an estimate as visible as the estimate itself. Replace fictional sample content with approved authored content before making product claims.',
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.tags.0": "uncertainty",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.tags.1": "confidence interval",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.tags.10": "untested assumption",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.tags.2": "bounds",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.tags.3": "error bars",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.tags.4": "range",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.tags.5": "point estimate",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.tags.6": "precision",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.tags.7": "reference value",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.tags.8": "small-sample limitation",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.tags.9": "scenario range",
  "motionAtlas.uncertainty-unfold.useWhen":
    "Make the limits around an estimate as visible as the estimate itself.",
