  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.creativeDirection":
    "960x600 React/SVG, shared palette, frame-driven 180 frames at 30fps. Frames 0-12 reveal the scene. Frames 13-50 reveal a two-measure wide table. Frames 51-110 peel the measure columns into vertical strips, carrying a subject-key copy with each cell. Frames 111-139 stack the strips as a long observation ledger with explicit measure and unit columns. Hold the resolved relationship at frames 140-165, then fade to the same opaque ground at 166-179. Reset is editorial.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.default.copy.context":
    "Fictional document",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.default.copy.result":
    "Extracted result",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.default.copy.source": "Original",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.default.measures.0.label": "Received",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.default.measures.0.unit": "crates",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.default.measures.1.label": "Used",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.default.measures.1.unit": "crates",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.default.subjects.0.label": "Site A",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.default.subjects.1.label": "Site B",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.description":
    "A wide table unfolds each measure column into its own observation row while repeating the correct subject and preserving the measurement name and unit.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.distinction":
    "Unlike source-merge, no datasets converge and no values are combined. Output grain changes from one row per subject to one row per subject-measure pair.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.domains.0": "Wide-to-long reshaping",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.goodFor.0":
    "Explain unpivoting wide measurements to a long table",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.goodFor.1":
    "Show how reshaping changes grain without creating measurements",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.heading.measure": "Measure",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.heading.subject": "Subject",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.heading.unit": "Unit",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.heading.value": "Value",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.intent":
    "Explain a change in measurement grain while preserving values.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.ledger": "Omitted missing cells",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.missing": "Missing",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.motionBeats.0": "Reveal the context.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.motionBeats.1":
    "Establish a two-measure wide table.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.motionBeats.2":
    "Peel measure strips into disjoint vertical lanes, then carry subject copies horizontally into one long ledger.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.motionBeats.3":
    "Hold explicit subject, measure, value and unit columns, optional source-cell keys and the omission ledger including zero-output cases. The outer renderer fades at 166..179.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.name":
    "Turn each measurement into a row",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.notFor.0":
    "A reshape is not a new observation or a recalculation.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.notFor.1":
    "Units may differ across measures and therefore must travel per row.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.notFor.2":
    "Duplicate subject labels remain distinct by ID.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.notFor.3":
    "No JSX, functions, URLs or external fetch in props. The animation is an authored explanation, not actual document extraction or product evidence.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.notFor.4":
    "Conservation counts only measurement cells: subjects.length*measures.length equals output measurement rows plus explicitly omitted missing measurement cells. Subject labels, headers and identifiers are not measurement cells.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.notFor.5":
    "Measure IDs and subject IDs are unique exact strings of maximum length 12 with no minimum. Each of exactly two subjects has exactly one value for each of exactly two existing measure IDs, independent of value-array order. Measurement pairs are unique. Measurement-cell count 4 = output rows + omitted null cells. Null never converts to zero. Units travel with the referenced measure.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.notFor.6":
    "Prose meaning is an author responsibility. Runtime validation enforces structural bounds, exact references and numeric/geometric rules.",
  "motionAtlas.wide-table-to-observations.prompt":
    'Use Motion Atlas "Turn each measurement into a row" (wide-table-to-observations) as an authored conceptual explanation. Explain a change in measurement grain while preserving values. Supply approved content before making product claims.',
